{"agent_id":"pp3g-Gfq8-diagnosis-fix-documentation-under-460-the-live-2bfc","agent_seq":6,"timestamp":"2026-08-25T07:01:15.063943469Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"1119c189-2781-4d21-bbc7-53157a03d0c2","comment_uuid":"f06796be-8107-4256-902c-3d7be02a7993","author":"pp3g-Gfq8-diagnosis-fix-documentation-under-460-the-live-2bfc","content":"SHAKEDOWN LEDGER (partial) - Observer v1 live shakedown n=1, night of 2026-08-25. Operator goal frame (quoted from dispatch): failure must become explicit, bounded, evidenced, and recoverable - never another archaeology exercise. A perfect run proves nothing; tonight's mixed run IS the deliverable.\n\nTABLE PASS - mechanisms that worked in production (evidence: /tmp/opencode/observer-state/events.jsonl unless noted):\n1. Evidence-bundle composition + sha256 manifesting: every terminal transition composed a 6-section bundle AT DETECTION with per-file sha256 (opencode-tail/pane-tail/git-status/git-diffstat/verdict-timeline/hub-position). Example event line 595: evidence-bundle agent=pp3g-YBKJ... path=.../20260825T055454Z-completed sha256{6}. 20 bundles in cycle 1; 19 bundle dirs on disk.\n2. Deliverable gate verification (#460 R2/FIX3): transition-action line 598 deliverable block branch=feature/pp3g-YBKJ... exists=true ahead_of_main=1 files_changed=1 sample_files=[to-file/ChatGPT Gastown Deep Dive Summary.md] deliverable_present=true. Gate also HELD cleanup for 14 completions with unverified deliverables (cleanup-skipped events lines 26-68 class; sweep reason completed-deliverable-unverified-worktree-preserved).\n3. Model-evidence staging row: model-evidence-row events + model-evidence-staging.jsonl (22.2KB) carrying agent/outcome/model/provider/deliverable/cleanup/evidence_sha256 per transition.\n4. Admission checks firing on dispatch: 86 checks in cycle 1, 778 more by 06:20; violations alerted to working issues ([OBSERVER][ADMISSION] comments 05:30-05:31 on #469/#462/#470 agents); audit trail in events.jsonl.\n5. DEAD-UNMARKED zombie detection with preserved forensics: lB2e 05:26:13 verdict FAILED reason='terminal verdict with only shell-level pane activity (zombie-prompt class)', worktree PRESERVED, bundle /tmp/opencode/observer-state/evidence/pp3g-lB2e-you-are-one-of-several-independent-adversarial-aed2/20260825T052613Z-failed (6 sha256 sections).\n6. Fail-safe worktree preservation on cleanup failure: when YBKJ cleanup was denied 05:54:54, Observer did NOT lose the worktree - orphan=true detected, force-sweep-flagged (line 596), preserved-worktrees recorded. This fail-safe is exactly why recovery was possible at all.\n\nTABLE FAIL->FIXED:\n1. Cleanup invocation failure. SYMPTOM: transition-action line 598 cleanup_ok=false orphan=true; healthy builder YBKJ deliverable-verified yet not cleaned. ROOT CAUSE (evidence-based): mutation-cap starvation + silent deny. action_window in manager-state.json held 24/24 entries (cap OBSERVER_MAX_ACTIONS_PER_HOUR=24) stamped 05:26:02..05:31:14 - consumed entirely by leftover-fleet triage comments. Rolling 1h window still saturated at 05:54:54 -> breaker_allow returned False -> kickoff_cleanup early-returned WITHOUT ANY EVENT (no subprocess ever ran; the once-per-hour breaker-halt event had already fired 05:31:38). The dispatch-suspected invocation form was PROVEN CORRECT: live dry-run 'crosslink kickoff cleanup --only pp3g-YBKJ-shakedown-healthy-builder-task-under-460-observer-is --dry-run --json --yes' rc=0 matched the agent exactly (status done, worktree+session identified). FIX commit 889570e7: breaker-deny path now emits event=cleanup denied=breaker-cap with reason in err - bounded, evidenced, never silent. Suite T20a reproduces the production state deterministically (pre-seeded full window -> deny must be loud, command must not run).\n2. Missing cleanup-event logging. SAME root cause, same fix: the out/err log_event never landed because the command never executed; the deny path had zero telemetry. Blast radius now quantified: ZERO comment events between 05:31:24 and 06:35 despite ~7 transition-actions (every completion/failure notification silently dropped while admission-checks kept flowing - Observer looked alive but its voice was cut). RECOVERY PROOF (task 4, through fixed code only): superseded pre-fix instance stopped 06:40 (FIX5 trap released lock cleanly on SIGHUP); YBKJ re-fire gate opened via surgical manager-state edit (handled.DONE-CONFIRMED removed, phase=active; pre-edit backup manager-state.pre-ybkj-refire.json kept); FIXED observer.sh --once ran against real fleet: evidence bundle .../20260825T064147Z-composed 06:41:47, cleanup event rc=0 out='Cleanup candidates: DONE pp3g-YBKJ... Killed tmux session...' 06:41:47.843, force-sweep-resolved event + resolved-by-cleanup-ok line appended to force-sweep-pending.txt, transition-action cleanup_ok=true orphan=false 06:41:58, completion comment posted to #460 06:41:58 ('Deliverable verified; scoped cleanup executed=yes'). Worktree and tmux session removed BY THE FIXED CODE PATH (crosslink invoked by observer.sh) - no hand-rm anywhere. Post-recovery state reconciled from event timestamps (the --once walk was killed mid-flight by my own shell timeout before its final save_state; YBKJ rec set to phase=completed handled[DONE-CONFIRMED]=06:41:58.176124 exactly as act_completed would have saved; relaunch confirmed zero duplicate actions).\n\nTABLE TRIAGED-DEFERRED:\n1. Admission retroactive false-positives on finished agents: [OBSERVER][ADMISSION] alerts raised against long-finished agents (2QW7/3Q1d/7zcB/Bi1p 05:30-05:31; my own finished agent Gfq8 flagged 06:35/06:42/06:54 incl. transient issue-claimed false positive that self-healed once the hub synced my lock). Admission policy currently re-checks every cycle against agents whose launch contracts are historical; needs a freshness/dispatch-time-only scope decision. NOT fixed here (policy, not bug).\n2. KICKOFF env-line model misparse: model IDs 'opencode/plugins' and 'opencode/observer-state' extracted as model-valid candidates and rejected against the live catalog - garbage IDs parsed from KICKOFF env lines rather than the actual --model flag. Parser fix deferred; does not affect supervision decisions today.\nAlso investigated and CLEARED: python-stderr.log NameError tracebacks (3x sys undefined) - mtime 2026-08-24 11:23, stale residue of the pre-launch build's test binary, unrelated to tonight; file untouched by the live run.\n\nSTATE AT HANDOFF: live supervision relaunched 06:47 on the FIXED binary (my worktree copy until orchestrator merges): PID 856975 holds observer.lock, first full cycle 06:54:12 rc=0 scanned=25 tracked=26 phases completed=18 failed=6 active=1 frozen-handled=1, zero fatal events, zero YBKJ duplicates. Commits this session: 889570e7 (fix + T20a/T20b; suite 122->130 green).\n\nWHY: tonight's mixed run converts the shakedown into the project demonstration record - one real production bug caught, root-caused with hard evidence, fixed with regression tests, and recovered through the fixed code path itself. WHAT: every claim above cites events.jsonl JSON, bundle paths, force-sweep/staging files, or commit 889570e7; recovery proven live (worktree+tmux removed by fixed code, orphan=false, sweep resolved, notification posted). HOW CERTAIN: evidence-based for all PASS/FAIL rows (direct observation of persisted artifacts); recovery certainty strong (cleanup rc=0 + physical verification of removal + hub comment). WHAT-NOT-TESTED: post_comment/kickoff_stop breaker-deny paths still return silently (same class as the fixed cleanup deny - proposed follow-up, not assigned so not changed); separate mutation budgets for comments vs follow-through actions (root-cause-class improvement, proposed for #460 discussion); rclone positive-path sync remains untested (remote unwired); long-duration multi-day loop behavior under the relaunched instance.","created_at":"2026-08-25T07:01:15.054307038Z","kind":"result","signed_by":"SHA256:K6HliG+FMpSzrkEs5c2elFvSm